WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.683
[MUSIC]

00:00:10.005 --> 00:00:15.768
Ask a lot of questions,
because the more information you have,

00:00:15.768 --> 00:00:18.876
the more power that you will have.

00:00:18.876 --> 00:00:26.448
Compensation has a lot more elements to
it, typically, than most people identify.

00:00:26.448 --> 00:00:31.044
At senior levels,
a compensation package is going to have

00:00:31.044 --> 00:00:34.969
maybe as many as eight or
ten major components.

00:00:34.969 --> 00:00:39.819
We tend to think about base salary,
cash incentive bonus,

00:00:39.819 --> 00:00:43.320
and equity grants, kind of the big three.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.923
But there's relocation allowances,

00:00:47.923 --> 00:00:50.992
home buying programmes,

00:00:50.992 --> 00:00:55.596
pension gross ups, signing bonuses.

00:00:55.596 --> 00:01:00.051
Special project based
incentive options and

00:01:00.051 --> 00:01:03.807
as many things as people can dream up.

00:01:03.807 --> 00:01:08.568
So the first thing you want to do when
you're in a compensation discussion with

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:13.488
anybody, is find out how many of those
elements might possibly come into play?

00:01:13.488 --> 00:01:16.218
Do you have project based bonuses?

00:01:16.218 --> 00:01:18.715
Do you do you use signing bonuses?

00:01:18.715 --> 00:01:22.747
How do you award option grants?

00:01:22.747 --> 00:01:25.313
If I'm relocating,
how do you deal with relocation?

00:01:25.313 --> 00:01:27.312
Is a home buyout part of that,
blah, blah, blah.

00:01:27.312 --> 00:01:32.758
And so, now you've got
a framework of what's possible.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:36.954
And there might be something on
that list that could be really,

00:01:36.954 --> 00:01:38.627
really valuable to you.

00:01:38.627 --> 00:01:44.472
If you go to work for Stanford,
your kids get to go to Stanford.

00:01:44.472 --> 00:01:46.446
I mean, if you got college aged kids,

00:01:46.446 --> 00:01:50.355
I mean, I know people who have stayed
here because of that, that's huge.

00:01:50.355 --> 00:01:53.999
And so find out what the list is.

00:01:53.999 --> 00:01:57.757
And then, the other thing,
I tell people, a compensation

00:01:57.757 --> 00:02:02.508
discussion is a little bit like working
at a mixing board in a sound studio.

00:02:02.508 --> 00:02:05.523
You ever see these things, they got all
these they're trying to manage the sound.

00:02:05.523 --> 00:02:08.097
Probably there's a guy back there
behind the wall doing that right now.

00:02:08.097 --> 00:02:12.624
And you got about ten levers that
various levels of the sound,

00:02:12.624 --> 00:02:17.425
you can't push them all to maximum
because you just get garbage.

00:02:17.425 --> 00:02:20.099
It's the same thing in
a compensation discussion,

00:02:20.099 --> 00:02:24.124
you can't push everything to maximum,
but you can probably push something.

00:02:24.124 --> 00:02:28.912
And one of the things, as I tell people,
try to find the soft money,

00:02:28.912 --> 00:02:30.091
if there is any.

00:02:30.091 --> 00:02:35.932
I mean, maybe the individual you're
talking to has a severe salary cap and

00:02:35.932 --> 00:02:38.447
they just can't go any higher.

00:02:38.447 --> 00:02:42.279
But they've got a lot of
discretion on a signing bonus.

00:02:42.279 --> 00:02:44.392
Well, money's money, okay?

00:02:44.392 --> 00:02:49.859
And so maybe you don't get that
extra 25 or $50,000 in salary,

00:02:49.859 --> 00:02:53.636
but you pick up $100,000 signing bonus.

00:02:53.636 --> 00:02:58.191
Well, that's pretty good because you
can have a salary negotiation again,

00:02:58.191 --> 00:02:58.870
in a year.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:04.851
But maybe you can negotiate it to six
months and get a review in six months.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.595
Again, what's the review cycle?

00:03:06.595 --> 00:03:09.600
That's one of the items on the list,
people don't tend to think about.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:14.451
So recognize at the end of
the day that if you push

00:03:14.451 --> 00:03:19.438
too many of the levers,
you could blow the deal.

00:03:19.438 --> 00:03:22.148
But you can push some, and
people expect you to push some money.

00:03:22.148 --> 00:03:28.117
And they're, I think, particularly
impressed, if you do it intelligently,

00:03:28.117 --> 00:03:33.233
particularly if you push something
that's not one of the top three.

00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:36.634
And if you've done your homework,
first off, I mean, at a minimum,

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:40.210
if you're replacing somebody,
you should be able to get everything that

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:43.745
that individual got, because that's
already been approved in the system.

00:03:43.745 --> 00:03:50.622
So that's a starting point and usually if
you ask, you can find out what that is.

00:03:50.622 --> 00:03:54.498
If you know what industry counterparts at
their competitors get for the same job,

00:03:54.498 --> 00:03:55.973
that's useful information.

00:03:55.973 --> 00:04:00.843
And so, again, do your homework,
figure out what the elements are.

00:04:00.843 --> 00:04:05.847
Push the one that in particular
is worth more to you to get,

00:04:05.847 --> 00:04:08.819
than it is to them to give it to you.

00:04:08.819 --> 00:04:13.390
And that's where you can really, if you
push on something where they're resisting,

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:14.649
that's going to be hard.

00:04:14.649 --> 00:04:17.073
So go find somewhere else.

00:04:17.073 --> 00:04:19.357
So it's another version
of an open door [LAUGH].

00:04:19.357 --> 00:04:21.499
But go find something that's easy,

00:04:21.499 --> 00:04:24.618
as opposed to fighting over
something that's hard.

00:04:24.618 --> 00:04:28.079
And I mean,
at the end of the day, I always,

00:04:30.349 --> 00:04:33.649
Try to encourage people
in that negotiation,

00:04:33.649 --> 00:04:39.159
to try to get the company to accept that
you want to bet on your own performance.

00:04:39.159 --> 00:04:45.665
So go for bigger upside on bonuses,
shorter reviews, project bonuses.

00:04:45.665 --> 00:04:47.933
Okay, I'll go in at this level,

00:04:47.933 --> 00:04:51.672
it's a little less than what
I want in terms of salary.

00:04:51.672 --> 00:04:57.334
But given that, is it possible that
I can have a review of six months?

00:04:57.334 --> 00:05:01.693
And if the performance warrants
I get that adjustment.

00:05:01.693 --> 00:05:06.020
That's pretty soft, they're not given
much, they're not giving away any money,

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:07.473
they may well agree to that.

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:10.425
And if you perform,
then you get it in six months.

00:05:10.425 --> 00:05:12.493
If you don't perform,
you weren't going to get it anyway.

00:05:12.493 --> 00:05:17.509
[MUSIC]

